269 0 obj
<<
  /Type /StructElem
  /S /Figure
  /P 268 0 R
  /Alt (This diagram illustrates the temporal coverage and data processing windows for a Copernicus Land Monitoring Service (CLMS) Level 2a (L2a) product update strategy, likely related to Persistent Scatterer Interferometry (PSI) or European Ground Motion Service (EGMS) data. The horizontal axis represents time, ranging from before 2015 to after 2023. The vertical axis represents an unspecified increasing value or measurement, with individual observations depicted as green triangles. The diagram shows four distinct temporal windows, each representing a processing period for product generation: 1. **Baseline:** Covers the period from 2015 to 2020, indicated by a light green rectangular block and a light green arrow. This window encompasses 9 visible data points (green triangles). 2. **1st Update:** Covers the period from 2015 to 2021, indicated by a light blue rectangular block and a light blue arrow. This window includes 10 visible data points, extending one year beyond the Baseline. 3. **2nd Update:** Covers the period from 2018 to 2022, indicated by a yellow rectangular block and a yellow arrow. This window includes 10 visible data points, starting later than the Baseline and 1st Update but extending further in time. 4. **3rd Update:** Covers the period from 2019 to 2023, indicated by a purple rectangular block and a purple arrow. This window includes 10 visible data points, starting later than the 2nd Update and extending one year further. Each update incorporates a specific time series of observations, depicted by the green triangles within its respective coloured rectangular block, demonstrating an incremental approach to maintaining and extending the product's temporal information.)
  /A [<<
    /O /Layout
    /Placement /Block
  >>]
  /K [0]
  /Pg 3100 0 R
>>
endobj

