428 0 obj
<<
  /Type /StructElem
  /S /Figure
  /P 427 0 R
  /Alt (This diagram illustrates the distribution of Measurement Points (MPs) within a 2x2 grid, representing data from 'Ascending' and 'Descending' Interferometric Synthetic Aperture Radar (InSAR) satellite acquisition geometries. Green grid cells indicate the presence of at least one Measurement Point, while light orange cells indicate the absence of Measurement Points for that specific acquisition geometry. In the 'Ascending' panel: * The top-left cell is green and contains one blue Measurement Point. * The top-right cell is light orange and contains no Measurement Points. * The bottom-left cell is light orange and contains no Measurement Points. * The bottom-right cell is green and contains one blue Measurement Point. In the 'Descending' panel: * The top-left cell is green and contains one orange Measurement Point. * The top-right cell is light orange and contains no Measurement Points. * The bottom-left cell is green and contains one orange Measurement Point. * The bottom-right cell is green and contains one orange Measurement Point. This representation is relevant to the Copernicus Land Monitoring Service (CLMS) European Ground Motion Service (EGMS) Ortho (L3) product, where ascending and descending datasets are gridded into a 100 m grid, and cells with at least one MP in each acquisition geometry are identified for subsequent decomposition into displacement vectors.)
  /A [<<
    /O /Layout
    /Placement /Block
  >>]
  /K [2]
  /Pg 3091 0 R
>>
