  /Type /StructElem
  /S /Figure
  /P 433 0 R
  /Alt (This conceptual spatial gridding diagram illustrates the distribution of measurement points (MP) from two different Interferometric Synthetic Aperture Radar (InSAR) acquisition geometries, 'Ascending' and 'Descending', within a uniform grid system. Each acquisition geometry is represented by a 2x2 grid, conceptually part of a larger 100 m grid used in the European Ground Motion Service (EGMS) Ortho product. For the 'Ascending' geometry, represented by blue circular points: - The top-left grid cell contains 11 points (green background). - The top-right grid cell contains 1 point (peach background). - The bottom-left grid cell contains 1 point (peach background). - The bottom-right grid cell contains 6 points (green background). For the 'Descending' geometry, represented by orange circular points: - The top-left grid cell contains 10 points (green background). - The top-right grid cell contains 3 points (peach background). - The bottom-left grid cell contains 9 points (green background). - The bottom-right grid cell contains 8 points (green background). The green background colour in cells indicates a higher density of measurement points, while the peach background indicates a lower density of points, demonstrating how raw InSAR data from different passes are spatially sampled and aggregated into grid cells for further processing.)
  /A [<<
    /O /Layout
    /Placement /Block
  >>]
  /K [0]
  /Pg 3091 0 R
