484 0 obj
<<
  /Type /StructElem
  /S /Figure
  /P 483 0 R
  /Alt (This conceptual diagram illustrates the decomposition of real 3D surface displacement (`d_real`) from Interferometric Synthetic Aperture Radar (InSAR) Line-Of-Sight (LOS) measurements. Two satellites are depicted: one in an 'LOS ascending' orbit and another in an 'LOS descending' orbit. Both satellites observe a single point on a curved grey surface, marked by a red dot, which is experiencing displacement. - The red vector `d_LOS Asc` represents the displacement component measured in the ascending Line-Of-Sight direction. - The blue vector `d_LOS Desc` represents the displacement component measured in the descending Line-Of-Sight direction. - The black vertical vector `d_v` indicates the vertical displacement component at the surface point. - The black dashed horizontal vector `d_WE` indicates the East-West displacement component. - The green vector `d_real` represents the actual 3D displacement vector of the surface point. The diagram visually depicts how the `d_real` displacement can be projected onto the Line-Of-Sight vectors of the ascending and descending satellites, yielding `d_LOS Asc` and `d_LOS Desc`, and how it relates to its vertical (`d_v`) and East-West (`d_WE`) components.)
  /A [<<
    /O /Layout
    /Placement /Block
  >>]
  /K [0]
  /Pg 3087 0 R
>>
endobj

