1153 0 obj
<<
  /Type /StructElem
  /S /Figure
  /P 1152 0 R
  /Alt (This image displays four scatter plots, labeled (a), (b), (c), and (d), each illustrating a time series of ground displacement measurements. The X-axis for all plots represents 'Time [days]' from 0 to 60 days, and the Y-axis represents 'Displacement [mm]' ranging from -30 mm to 10 mm. Each subplot shows: * Blue dots: Individual displacement measurements over time. * Red line: A linear regression model fitted to the displacement data. * Green circle: A specific highlighted data point. In all four plots, the displacement data points generally show a linear decreasing trend, indicating subsidence. * **Plot (a):** Initial displacement is approximately +7 mm at Time 0 days, decreasing to around -20 mm at Time 60 days. The green circle highlights a data point near 15 days with a displacement of 0 mm. * **Plot (b):** Initial displacement is approximately +5 mm at Time 0 days, decreasing to around -22 mm at Time 60 days. The green circle highlights a data point near Time 0 days with a displacement of approximately +1 mm. * **Plot (c):** Initial displacement is approximately +5 mm at Time 0 days, decreasing to around -20 mm at Time 60 days. The green circle highlights a data point near 22 days with a displacement of 0 mm. * **Plot (d):** Initial displacement is approximately +5 mm at Time 0 days, decreasing to around -25 mm at Time 60 days. The green circle highlights a data point near Time 0 days with a displacement of approximately +1 mm. The charts depict ground deformation consistent with Interferometric Synthetic Aperture Radar (InSAR) derived data, often processed by services like the European Ground Motion Service (EGMS), showing linear ground subsidence over a 60-day period.)
  /A [<<
    /O /Layout
    /Placement /Block
  >>]
  /K [0]
  /Pg 2999 0 R
>>
