1628 0 obj
<<
  /Type /StructElem
  /S /Figure
  /P 1627 0 R
  /Alt (This diagram illustrates a process flow for Interferometric Synthetic Aperture Radar (InSAR) data processing, specifically focusing on geometric co-registration and subsequent analysis steps. The process begins with **Master Selection**, which identifies a primary image from **S1 Images** (Sentinel-1 Synthetic Aperture Radar images). The output of this selection is a **Master Image**. This **Master Image**, along with **S1 Images**, **Orbits**, and a **DEM** (Digital Elevation Model), are inputs to the **Geometric Co-Registration** step. Following geometric co-registration, the data proceeds to **Spectral Diversity** analysis. The final step shown is **Overlapping areas data analysis**, which takes its input from the spectral diversity results. The flow indicates that master image selection is a prerequisite for the accurate geometric co-registration of SAR imagery.)
  /A [<<
    /O /Layout
    /Placement /Block
  >>]
  /K [0]
  /Pg 2964 0 R
>>
endobj

