1673 0 obj
<<
  /Type /StructElem
  /S /Figure
  /P 1672 0 R
  /Alt (This is an Interferometric Synthetic Aperture Radar (InSAR) processing workflow diagram for ground motion monitoring. The process integrates two primary inputs: SAR Images (Synthetic Aperture Radar Images) and a Digital Elevation Model (DEM). The workflow proceeds through the following sequential steps: 1. **SAR Images** are used for **Reference Image Selection**. 2. The selected reference images undergo **Co-Registration**. 3. The co-registered images are then combined with the **DEM** to generate a **Differential Interferogram**. 4. From the differential interferogram, **MPs Candidates** (Measurement Points Candidates) are identified. 5. These candidates are used to establish a **Geodetic Network**. 6. The geodetic network data is then processed through **Phase Unwrapping**. 7. This is followed by **Atmospheric Processing**. 8. Next is **MP (PS/DS) Identification**, which refers to the identification of Measurement Points as either Pointwise Scatterers (PS) or Distributed Scatterers (DS). 9. **Side Lobes Removal** is performed. 10. The data is then subjected to **Geocoding**. 11. The final output of the geocoding step constitutes the **Deliverables**.)
  /A [<<
    /O /Layout
    /Placement /Block
  >>]
  /K [21]
  /Pg 2960 0 R
>>
endobj

